# tabbing-on tour

## Ported from tabbing-on's script.md demo script.
## Requires tabbing-on installed and on PATH — demo-runner picks up the
## integration automatically when the tabbing-on shell adapter is found.

# Act 1: Setup & Help

$ eval "$(tabbing-init zsh)"

$ tabbing-on help

## What emojis and colors are available?

$ tabbing-on emojis

$ tabbing-on colors

# Act 2: Basic Title & Status

## Set a tab title with emoji, color highlight, and urgency.
## Watch your terminal's tab as each command runs.

$ tabbing-on "The Great American Novel" -blue "Pick Genre" -rocket

$ tabbing-on

$ tabbing-status -brain "Research Train Schedules"

$ tabbing-status -fire "Write hype blog"

$ tabbing-on "Expunge Novel Plans" -red "Holding back tears" -pri0

$ tabbing-on

# Act 3: Todo Management

## Start a real project and add subtasks.

$ tabbing-on "Acme Dashboard" -green "Planning" -gear -pri4

$ tabbing-todo "K8 infra setup" -e gear -m "Deploy to staging cluster"

$ tabbing-todo "UX Design" -e art -m "Figma mockups"

$ tabbing-todo

## Pick one to work on (piped answer stands in for the interactive prompt).

$ echo "1" | tabbing-todo --pick

$ tabbing-on

## Mark it done, pick the next.

$ tabbing-todo --done

$ tabbing-on

# Act 4: Recording

## Create a sample .cast recording and play it back with asciinema.

$ _tabbing_demo_create_sample_cast

$ tabbing-recordings

$ _tabbing_demo_play_recording

# Act 5: Terminal Detection

$ tabbing-on --terminal-info

# Act 6: History & Reporting

## Every title/status change is logged with timestamps.

$ tabbing-report

## Same data as Mermaid syntax — paste into docs.

$ tabbing-report --mermaid

$ tabbing-history "Novel"

# Act 7: Full Info Dump

$ tabbing-info

@prompt Press Enter to finish...
